        The source code for a work means the preferred form of the work
for making modifications to it.  It must include all the relevant
source code and any other information necessary to modify the work
and compile it.  It must not be limited to a particular environment
or to particular facilities.  For example, if the work is a program,
the source code must include the source code for all the modules it
contains, plus any associated interface definition files, plus the
scripts used to control compilation and installation of the program.

        The source code for a work must be made available to the same
persons to whom you make the work available under the terms of this
License.  You must cause all persons to whom you convey or otherwise
make available the unmodified Program or a covered work, to receive
the source code on a medium customarily used for software interchange.

If you distribute the program (or any work based on the program) as
part of a user product, and the user product depends on the unmodified
program or a covered work to function, you must cause the source code
to be made available to the user through a network server at no charge
to the user, using one of the methods in this License.

